# What EAS Build uploads. Repo root only — a .easignore anywhere else is ignored.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING — two traps, both of which have already bitten:
#
# 1. This file REPLACES every .gitignore in the repo. It does not add to them. So
#    anything not listed here IS uploaded, including files git has always ignored.
#    That is why node_modules/ and .env appear below despite being gitignored:
#    deleting a line here does not fall back to .gitignore, it starts uploading.
#
# 2. A pattern without a leading slash matches at EVERY depth. `design/` looks like
#    it means the repo-root design/ folder; it also matches mobile/src/design/ and
#    silently drops tokens.ts, which every screen imports — the build then fails in
#    `expo export:embed` with no useful message. Anchor root-relative paths with a
#    leading slash. Keep this list short: the size win is almost entirely
#    node_modules/ and mobile/android/, and every extra pattern is another chance
#    to delete something the bundler needs.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Env values reach the build through eas.json's `env` block and EAS Secrets,
# never through an uploaded file (CLAUDE.md constraint #4).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- dependencies (5.4 GB) — reinstalled on the build machine ----------------
node_modules/

# --- native projects (4.0 GB) ------------------------------------------------
# Continuous Native Generation: android/ and ios/ are build output, not source.
# They are gitignored and app.config.ts is the source of truth for every plugin
# and permission, so EAS runs `expo prebuild` to regenerate them.
/mobile/android/
/mobile/ios/
/mobile/.expo/

# --- deployed separately, not compiled into the app --------------------------
/backend/
/docs/

# --- binaries and local noise ------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.exe
*.log
